# Personal-use apt packages — desktop, server, wsl. NOT wsl-work.
# Installed by: setup/modules/00-apt-base.sh (every profile except wsl-work)
# Docs:         docs/setup/wsl-work.md
#
# Each entry is here because it only serves a personal tool or use case that
# does not belong on a company machine. Add a line to base.list only if it
# would pass review at the workplace; otherwise it belongs here.

# Claude Code's sandboxed Bash tool needs both on Linux; without them the CLI
# still runs but warns, and sandboxing is unavailable. The CLI itself is not an
# apt package here: setup/modules/28-claude-code.sh (which warns if these are
# missing, since it can run without 00-apt-base). socat is also a generic
# relay/tunnel tool, another reason to keep it off a work box. bin/mpv-ipc and
# bin/tts-speak use it too, desktop only.
bubblewrap
socat
